{% psec 1, "Does Yesterday's Move Undo Itself?", "What did I set out to test?", "Overview" %}
<p class="topic-intro">
  This started with a MemLabs YouTube tutorial. It bet against every daily move in Bitcoin Cash: buy after a down day, sell after an up day. Over four years it showed a Sharpe ratio of about \(0.94\). I rebuilt the idea for the markets I want to trade, EURUSD, USDJPY, gold and oil. First I fixed the problems I found in the original. Then I kept going, one stage at a time, until something either clearly worked or clearly didn't.
</p>
